# ---- Interim: copy to .env and adjust. No secrets are required for the demo. ----
# Who reads this file:
#   - The API (`make api`, `make dev`, `npm run api`) loads it itself; shell variables win.
#   - make (`make dev`, `make bridge`) picks ONLY these keys out of it and exports them to the
#     bridge and API: API_HOST API_PORT VITALS_SOURCE VITALS_SCENARIO VITALS_MIN_CONF BRIDGE_TOKEN
#     BRIDGE_WS_HOST BRIDGE_WS_PORT BRIDGE_API_URL BRIDGE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS SERIALPORT
#     PRESAGE_API_KEY PRESAGE_CAMERA_ID. Precedence: `make VAR=x` > shell > .env > defaults.
#     Plain KEY=value lines only: no quotes, no `$` or `#` inside values.
#   - The bridge itself never reads .env (no dotenv). `npm run bridge` / `npm run dev` from the
#     root do NOT apply it either: they always run the mock source with defaults. Use make, or
#     export the variables in your shell, for anything else.
#   - `docker compose` reads it only to fill ${VAR:-default} placeholders in docker-compose.yml;
#     a variable reaches a container only when docker-compose.yml lists it (PRESAGE_* never does).
#   - Vite does NOT read it (its envDir is apps/web); see the Web section at the bottom.

# ---- API ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bind address and port for `make api` / `make dev` (uvicorn). The Vite dev proxy expects :8000.
API_HOST=0.0.0.0
API_PORT=8000
# SQLite by default (relative paths resolve against the repo root). Postgres example:
# postgresql+psycopg://interim:interim@db:5432/interim
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./data/runtime/interim.db
# Shared demo password for the three seeded users (coordinator, investigator, admin).
DEMO_PASSWORD=interim-demo
# Secret used to sign session tokens. Change in any real deployment.
AUTH_SECRET=change-me-in-production
# Bearer token lifetime in hours.
TOKEN_TTL_HOURS=12
# Optional shared secret the vitals bridge sends as X-Bridge-Token. Empty = not enforced, and
# then no HTTP caller may post isMeasured=true samples (a real sensor needs it set on both sides).
# `make dev` hands the same value to the API and the bridge; a bridge started any other way
# needs BRIDGE_TOKEN in its own environment (or --token), or every vitals POST gets 401.
BRIDGE_TOKEN=
# Comma-separated CORS origins for the web app in dev (nginx proxies /api in Docker).
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
# Seed the demo study/participants/notes on first start if the DB is empty.
SEED_ON_START=true
# POST /admin/reset wipes every table, audit chain included. Demo instances only.
ALLOW_DEMO_RESET=true
# Demo study to display (public ClinicalTrials.gov record, cached under data/public/).
DEMO_NCT_ID=NCT03088540
# info | debug | warning
LOG_LEVEL=info
# Where study.json and the LIBTAYO label excerpt are read from (default: <repo>/data/public).
# PUBLIC_DATA_DIR=

# ---- Vitals bridge (runs on the kiosk machine) ---------------------------------------------
# mock | presage | arduino
VITALS_SOURCE=mock
# resting | post_exercise | tachypnea | low_quality | dropout
VITALS_SCENARIO=resting
# Pin the confidence threshold; leave unset to adopt the API's value (rules tables).
# VITALS_MIN_CONF=0.6
BRIDGE_WS_PORT=8787
# Bind address: loopback by default; 0.0.0.0 for Docker or a kiosk on another device.
BRIDGE_WS_HOST=127.0.0.1
BRIDGE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
# Browser origins allowed to open the bridge WebSocket (comma-separated). Empty = any for
# `make dev`; under docker compose empty means the compose web app's own origins only
# (http://localhost:5173, http://127.0.0.1:5173).
BRIDGE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# Arduino source only (stub): serial port of the sensor sketch.
SERIALPORT=
# Presage source only (implemented; needs `npm run install:presage` in apps/vitals-bridge).
# API key from physiology.presagetech.com. Keep it out of git; it is never passed to Docker.
PRESAGE_API_KEY=
# Optional camera id from `npm run bridge -- --source presage --list-cameras` (required on Windows).
PRESAGE_CAMERA_ID=

# ---- Web (Vite) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not read from this file. The web app talks to the API via /api (dev proxy or nginx) and to the
# bridge over WS at ws://<page hostname>:8787 unless VITE_BRIDGE_WS_URL is set; to change it in
# dev, put `VITE_BRIDGE_WS_URL=ws://host:port` in apps/web/.env.local. In Docker use
# DOCKER_BRIDGE_WS_URL below (baked in at image build time).

# ---- Optional Claude writer (apps/api/interim_api/writers; packets track) -----------
# Empty (default) = the deterministic template writer writes every narrative and brief.
# When set, Claude rephrases the template draft and its text is kept only if
# validate_written passes (every evidence id resolves, quotes verbatim, 'investigator to
# confirm' on grades), else the template text is used with a stated fallback reason.
# Needs: pip install -e "apps/api[llm]".
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# INTERIM_WRITER=auto
# INTERIM_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# ---- Docker compose only --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host interface the published ports bind to. 127.0.0.1 (default) keeps the stack off the venue
# network; the demo password and AUTH_SECRET above are public. For a kiosk on another device use
# 0.0.0.0, and change AUTH_SECRET + DEMO_PASSWORD and set BRIDGE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS first.
# INTERIM_BIND=127.0.0.1
# Host ports (container ports are fixed). Moving the bridge port also needs DOCKER_BRIDGE_WS_URL.
# INTERIM_API_PORT=8000
# INTERIM_WEB_PORT=5173
# INTERIM_BRIDGE_PORT=8787
# Database URL inside the api container (default: SQLite in the `interim-db` volume).
# DOCKER_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////var/lib/interim/interim.db
# Bridge WebSocket URL baked into the web image at build time (empty = ws://<page hostname>:8787).
# DOCKER_BRIDGE_WS_URL=
